{"chunk_id": "50bb94d0a01c", "text": "This section recounts the continuation of the royal line of Sagara and the origin of Bhagiratha\u2019s famous quest. After Ansuman and his son Dilipa fail to bring the sacred river Ganga to earth to redeem Sagara\u2019s sixty thousand sons\u2014burned to ashes by the sage Kapila\u2014Bhagiratha becomes king. Learning of his ancestors\u2019 tragic fate, he renounces royal comfort and undertakes severe austerities in the Himalayas. The narrative dwells on the grandeur of the mountain landscape, emphasizing the sacred setting of his penance. After a thousand years of ascetic practice, the goddess Ganga appears and offers him a boon. Bhagiratha asks her to descend to earth so her waters may purify his forefathers\u2019 remains and grant them heaven. Ganga agrees but warns that only the god Siva can withstand the force of her descent, sending Bhagiratha to seek Siva\u2019s aid.\nBhagiratha performs long austerities to bring Ganga to earth to liberate Sagara\u2019s sons; Ganga agrees but says only Shiva can bear her descent.\nThemes: filial duty, austerity and penance, divine intervention, sacred river Ganga, liberation of ancestors", "vector": [0.010831811465322971, -0.01225811243057251, -0.004144345410168171, 0.02249787375330925, -0.0015970193780958652, 0.03081347607076168, -0.02927953004837036, 0.008948017843067646, -0.02930644154548645, -0.017842212691903114, -0.005489911884069443, 0.022874632850289345, 0.015191446989774704, 0.01912050135433674, 0.0021226312965154648, -0.009910098277032375, 0.042815931141376495, -0.019537627696990967, 0.02171744592487812, -0.005207343026995659, 0.0021243132650852203, -0.010616520419716835, 0.0014498480595648289, 0.018636098131537437, -0.038510117679834366, 0.01427646167576313, 0.024623868986964226, -0.026669131591916084, 0.010024471208453178, 0.001488533103838563, -0.026157815009355545, -0.005802756175398827, -0.00898838508874178, -0.0028290539048612118, -0.009876458905637264, -0.00112859404180198